# Recorded deficiencies — human-authorised descopes only.
#
# ── Drained 2026-07-26 ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# EMPTY IS THE CORRECT STATE. An empty log means the work was done, or it is
# tracked somewhere a human will actually see it. An empty log is not suspicious
# and is not a sign of insufficient self-criticism; honesty is demonstrated by
# the diff, not by the length of this file.
#
# This file had grown to ~69 dated blocks / 2040 lines carrying exactly ONE
# real `Decided-by:` line. Every block was triaged:
#
#   * operational / environmental notes (machine load, budget, killed
#     processes, "delegated to CI", gate narration)
#                                                 -> deleted, never belonged here
#   * entries later resolved, in-file or by a
#     subsequent landing                          -> deleted, nothing to record
#   * duplicates and superseded blocks            -> deleted
#   * design boundaries with no forward path      -> deleted, not deficiencies
#   * live shortfalls with a real forward path    -> FILED as GitHub issues
#                                                    #1644–#1657, plus comments
#                                                    on #1443, #1530, #1642 and
#                                                    PR #1626
#
# Several entries had gone stale unnoticed, which is the point: the >50 MB
# generated-artifact problem, the vendored structured-zstd override and its
# `[patch.crates-io]` block were all already resolved by later work while their
# entries sat here unread.
#
# Process for the next drain: .agents/skills/deficiency-cleanup/SKILL.md
#
# ── Format ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One dated block per entry. Every entry MUST carry a real `Decided-by:` line
# naming the human who authorised the descope and quoting their answer:
#
#   =========================================================================
#   ## From #<issue> — <title> (recorded <YYYY-MM-DD>)
#   <merge/PR ref + one-line state>
#
#   D1. <one-line deficiency>.
#       Decided-by: <human> on <YYYY-MM-DD> — asked "<the binary you put to
#                   them>", answered "<their verbatim answer>".
#       <what is less than maximal in the SHIPPED CODE>
#       Forward path: <the real work that would close it, and where it is
#                     tracked>.
#
# No `Decided-by:` line means it is not an entry. Do the work, or ask.
#
# Nothing in this repo reads this file. Recording here does not schedule the
# work, does not track it, and does not tell anyone — so every entry must also
# be surfaced on the issue and the PR, and stated plainly in the completion
# report. Three entries for one issue means the issue was not implemented:
# stop and say so.
